{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyKJFC3darmFFznLGdH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't confirm whether Cloudflare officially calls it \"beta\" anymore. In the installed wrangler 4.148.0 it works like a default feature. The `--experimental-provision` flag (alias `--x-provision`) defaults to `true` and is hidden from help (`node_modules/wrangler/wrangler-dist/cli.js:361358`). Its description still says \"Experimental: Enable automatic resource provisioning\", which is probably left over from earlier versions.\n\nSo `wrangler deploy` provisions resources without any opt-in flag. According to the project's Ludion notes, since 4.113.0 that also covers Queue, Dispatch Namespace and Flagship bindings, so you can leave out the resource name or ID. If you need to know whether it's officially \"beta\", Cloudflare's docs and changelog are the place to check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1204,"cache_read_input_tokens":71321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1204},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95369737-68af-4370-8a34-8d0268482c49","uuid":"8556d740-0b4d-4b66-a936-8f985e3c394b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:05.519Z","request_id":"req_011CfwyKHyZr7Q7mk3T8xCok"}
